@page "/script"

<GalleryPage Title="Script">
    <Lede>Three controls on plain HTML. The library script keeps their state in step with the browser, even on a static page.</Lede>

    <Section Title="Popover">
        <p>Open the note, then press Escape to close it. The button reports whether the note is expanded.</p>
        <Demo>
            <button class="fl-button" type="button" id="script-trigger" popovertarget="script-popover" aria-expanded="false">Show note</button>
            <div class="fl-popover" id="script-popover" popover="auto">
                <div class="fl-popover__body"><p>This note stays open until you dismiss it.</p></div>
            </div>
        </Demo>
    </Section>

    <Section Title="Mixed checkbox">
        <p>The dash means that some items are selected. Press Space or select the label to choose all items.</p>
        <Demo>
            <div class="fl-checkbox">
                <input class="fl-checkbox__control" type="checkbox" id="script-checkbox" data-fl-indeterminate />
                <label class="fl-checkbox__label" for="script-checkbox">Select all items</label>
            </div>
        </Demo>
    </Section>

    <Section Title="Number input">
        <p>Choose a quantity from 0 to 2. Use the minus and plus buttons, or the arrow keys in the field. Each button stops at its limit.</p>
        <Demo Column>
            <div class="fl-field">
                <label class="fl-field__label" for="script-number">Quantity</label>
                <span class="fl-input fl-number-input gallery-narrow">
                    <input class="fl-input__control fl-number-input__control" type="number" id="script-number"
                           min="0" max="2" step="1" data-fl-value="@_quantity" @bind="_quantity" @onflsamplechange="OnSampleChange" />
                    <button class="fl-number-input__step" type="button" tabindex="-1" aria-label="Decrease"><svg class="fl-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="design/icons/lucide.svg#minus" /></svg></button>
                    <button class="fl-number-input__step" type="button" tabindex="-1" aria-label="Increase"><svg class="fl-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="design/icons/lucide.svg#plus" /></svg></button>
                </span>
            </div>
            <div>Bound value: <output id="script-bound-value" for="script-number">@_quantity</output></div>
            <div>Value from the sample event: <output id="script-event-value" for="script-number">@_eventValue</output></div>
            <div><button class="fl-button" type="button" id="script-set-one" disabled="@(!RendererInfo.IsInteractive)" @onclick="() => _quantity = 1">Set quantity to 1 from .NET</button></div>
        </Demo>
        <p>In server and WebAssembly modes, .NET receives the native change and a typed sample event for the same field. The last button sets the quantity from .NET instead. In static mode only the field changes and the last button is disabled.</p>
    </Section>
</GalleryPage>

@code {
    private int _quantity = 1;
    private string? _eventValue = "No change yet";

    private void OnSampleChange(ChangeEventArgs args) => _eventValue = args.Value?.ToString();
}
